  "rationale": "The plant automata G1 models the robot's perception of obstacles and its motion capabilities, with open-loop controllable actions and uncontrollable sensor events. The specification automata E1 enforces conservative exploration: random_walk is used in clear states, move_forward is only allowed in a dedicated commit state, and obstacle events force deterministic turn-based recovery. Obstacle recovery states only allow a single turn action and never random_walk or move_forward. All uncontrollable events are total in every state. The design ensures safe, steady exploration with reliable obstacle avoidance and no infinite controllable loops.",
